- Complete list of Olympus Pro partners beyond the 4 announced (Frax, Lido, Tokemak, Rari) — docs mention "partners" generically but no updated public list
- Vercel/Netlify frontend hosting — inferred from Next.js usage but not explicitly confirmed in sources
- Grant program existence — forum and blog show no official grant program; unclear if ecosystem fund exists
- Hackathon participation / developer outreach programs — not documented in official sources
- Third-party applications using Olympus SDK — SDK exists but no public registry of integrations
- Cross-chain bridge partnerships (LayerZero, Wormhole, Axelar, etc.) — V3 "multi-chain native" but no native bridge; third-party bridge support not documented
- Oracle redundancy / fallback plans — only Chainlink documented; no evidence of Chainlink backup or alternative oracle (TWAP, custom)
- Guardian multi-sig composition (signers, threshold) — only "Gnosis Safe" mentioned without details
- Treasury multi-sig composition (signers, threshold) — same as above
- Formal verification status — no Certora/runtime verification evidence in public audit directories
- Testnet deployments (Sepolia, Arbitrum Sepolia, Base Sepolia) for V3 — not documented; CI/CD may use Anvil/fork only
- MEV protection for bonding/staking — not documented in tech specs or audits
- Disaster recovery / emergency shutdown procedures — guardian pause documented but full recovery process not public
- Client diversity — only single frontend (olympus-frontend) documented; no mobile app, CLI, alternative clients
- Dependency audit for transitive dependencies (OpenZeppelin, Solmate, etc.) — not separately documented